Topic. 1: VIEW - A view merges required columns from multiple tables to create a virtual table for simpler querying and better data visualization,
                 without actually copying or storing duplicate data.

Example -  wriet query to display title, released_year, genre, first_name, last_name.

SELECT 
    title, released_year, genre, rating, first_name, last_name
FROM
    reviews rs
        JOIN
    series s ON s.id = rs.series_id
        JOIN
    reviewers rr ON rr.id = rs.reviewers_id;

-- Now using the O/P from above query create a separate virtual table 

create view master_review 
AS
SELECT 
    title, released_year, genre, rating, first_name, last_name
FROM
    reviews rs
        JOIN
    series s ON s.id = rs.series_id
        JOIN
    reviewers rr ON rr.id = rs.reviewers_id;
